---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Clear explanation of what data Retenqo's website, hosting provider, GitHub Releases, and Android app process."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <p
      class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-[var(--accent-primary)] uppercase"
    >
      Privacy
    </p>
    <h1
      class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-4xl"
    >
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
      Retenqo is built on a simple principle: your personal memories belong on
      your device. This policy explains what happens across the website,
      hosting, APK distribution, and Android app.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)]">
      Last reviewed: November 25, 2026
    </p>

    <div
      class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--text-secondary)]"
    >
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          1. This Website
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          This static website does not use tracking cookies, third-party
          advertising, user fingerprinting, or analytics scripts. We do not
          collect personal information or run user accounts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          2. Hosting &amp; Network Requests
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The website is served as static files over HTTPS via Cloudflare Pages.
          Like any web host, Cloudflare may process standard HTTP request
          metadata (such as IP address and user agent) for security, DDoS
          protection, and routing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          3. APK Downloads via GitHub Releases
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          When you click to download the Android APK, your browser connects
          directly to GitHub Releases. GitHub's own privacy policy applies to
          that download request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          4. The Retenqo Android Application
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Memories and commitments are stored in a local Room database encrypted
          with SQLCipher. A random database key is wrapped by a non-exportable
          Android Keystore key. OCR, memory search, and AI inference run on the
          device after any optional model download.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Pending notification content and ordinary settings are stored in
          app-private preferences but are not application-level encrypted. The
          Android app sandbox still applies. Notification capture is paused by
          default; only source groups you enable are queued. Revoking a source
          removes its pending items before further processing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          5. How personal content moves
        </h2>
        <figure
          class="mt-4 rounded-2xl border p-4"
          style="border-color: var(--border-subtle); background: var(--bg-secondary);"
        >
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 960 250"
            role="img"
            aria-labelledby="privacy-flow-title privacy-flow-desc"
            class="h-auto w-full"
          >
            <title id="privacy-flow-title">
              Retenqo processes selected content locally
            </title>
            <desc id="privacy-flow-desc"
              >Selected messages, images, and voice enter the Android phone,
              local OCR and inference process them, and memories are saved in
              the SQLCipher database.</desc
            >
            <defs>
              <linearGradient id="flow-line" x1="0" x2="1">
                <stop stop-color="#67d8ff"></stop><stop
                  offset="1"
                  stop-color="#5ee8bd"></stop>
              </linearGradient>
            </defs>
            <rect
              x="16"
              y="40"
              width="230"
              height="168"
              rx="24"
              fill="#111a29"
              stroke="#233249"
              stroke-width="2"></rect>
            <rect
              x="365"
              y="40"
              width="230"
              height="168"
              rx="24"
              fill="#111a29"
              stroke="#233249"
              stroke-width="2"></rect>
            <rect
              x="714"
              y="40"
              width="230"
              height="168"
              rx="24"
              fill="#111a29"
              stroke="#233249"
              stroke-width="2"></rect>
            <path
              d="M256 124h92m-14-14 14 14-14 14M605 124h92m-14-14 14 14-14 14"
              fill="none"
              stroke="url(#flow-line)"
              stroke-width="5"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
            <g
              fill="none"
              stroke="#67d8ff"
              stroke-width="4"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
            >
              <path d="M81 112h70v50H81zM93 99h70v50M105 86h70v50"></path>
              <path d="M426 88h108v78H426zM446 108h68M446 126h50M446 144h38"
              ></path>
              <path
                d="M776 93h104a10 10 0 0 1 10 10v66a10 10 0 0 1-10 10h-104a10 10 0 0 1-10-10v-66a10 10 0 0 1 10-10zM792 118h72M792 139h52"
              ></path>
            </g>
            <text
              x="131"
              y="190"
              text-anchor="middle"
              fill="#f1f5f9"
              font-family="sans-serif"
              font-size="16">Your selected content</text
            >
            <text
              x="480"
              y="190"
              text-anchor="middle"
              fill="#f1f5f9"
              font-family="sans-serif"
              font-size="16">Local OCR and AI</text
            >
            <text
              x="829"
              y="190"
              text-anchor="middle"
              fill="#f1f5f9"
              font-family="sans-serif"
              font-size="16">Encrypted Room database</text
            >
          </svg>
          <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs" style="color: var(--text-muted);">
            The notification queue is a temporary exception: its pending text is
            local but not application-encrypted.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          6. Retention and deletion
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Saved memories remain until you delete them or use Delete all personal
          data in Settings. That action also clears queued notifications,
          background ingest work, media history, temporary selected-media files,
          and the volatile screen snapshot. Disabling a notification source
          stops new capture and causes its queued items to be removed before
          processing. Android app data removal or uninstall removes app-private
          data, but we cannot promise forensic erasure from flash storage.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Encrypted backup files are user-controlled exports. Retenqo cannot
          delete copies you saved elsewhere; remove those separately. Keep a
          backup before major updates and store its password safely.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          7. External providers
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The website is hosted by Cloudflare Pages. APK downloads connect to
          GitHub Releases. If you choose to download the optional model, the
          device connects to Hugging Face. Those providers may receive ordinary
          request metadata under their own policies. Personal memory content is
          not sent in these requests by the app.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
